From 4e8fb5b90001a3c7d0d74c65c7defc2dd3d90747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:59:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/52] fix-sec-3: S-10: bounded Meta, job-family and DOL
 parsers (linear on hostile text, same output on real data)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- meta.js parseMetaAmount: trimmed, first 100 characters; parseMetaSitemap: <loc>[^<]{0,2048}</loc>;
  JSON-LD: metaJsonLd, one forward pass (type attribute within 500 characters of <script).
- families.js prep: first 500 characters, brackets [（(][^（(）)]{0,200}[）)].
- scripts/alt-data/xlsx.js: cellElements / textRuns / dropPhonetic replace CELL_RE and the rich-text
  regexes with forward scans that match exactly what they matched; employers.js: names capped at 300.
Tests: the three S-10 to-dos un-todo'd; test/fix-sec-3.test.js times 64-256 KB hostile inputs of every
shape (under 2 s; 2 to 60 s before) and checks old versus new output on the real fixtures and on
seeded fuzz (all equal). familyOfTitle is unchanged on all 37,619 titles of today's crawl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
